;;; `iterate' is gone. It walked a haskell Vector -- cloning it for the
;;; duration, opening the box, then stepping a begin/end pair -- and there is
;;; no Vector any more. A std vector is walked with an index and its `len',
;;; and a std string the same way; see lib/std/vector.cicili.
